# Production hosting (AWS + GitHub)

SchoolTime production does **not** use Render. Do not add Render URLs, `render.yaml` deploy steps, or `onrender.com` examples to new docs or env templates.

## Canonical stack

| Layer | Service |
|-------|---------|
| SPA | **GitHub Pages** — `deploy-pages.yml` on `main`; repo variable **`VITE_API_BASE_URL`** = `https://<api-host>/api` |
| API | **EC2** — Docker image from root **`Dockerfile`**; bind **`HOST=0.0.0.0`**, **`PORT=8787`** |
| DB | **RDS PostgreSQL** — `DB_CLIENT=postgres` |
| HTTPS | **Caddy** on EC2 → `reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8787` |

No custom domain: use **DuckDNS** (e.g. `schooltime-api.duckdns.org`) — see `docs/AWS_FREE_TIER_SETUP.md` Part 5.

## EC2 `.env` (Docker + RDS)

- `NODE_ENV=production`
- `DATABASE_URL` — **no** `?sslmode=require` in the URL when using the Node `pg` pool on Docker (pg v8+ treats it as strict TLS). Use host path only, e.g. `postgresql://USER:PASS@endpoint:5432/postgres`. RDS Easy Create often creates DB **`postgres`**, not `schooltime` — check RDS **Configuration → DB name**.
- `CORS_ORIGIN` — exact GitHub Pages origin (e.g. `https://rahul-vik.github.io`, no trailing slash)
- `APP_BASE_URL` — full SPA path (e.g. `https://rahul-vik.github.io/SchoolTime`)
- API container: `-p 127.0.0.1:8787:8787` (public HTTPS via Caddy only)

`server/db.js` strips SSL query params from `DATABASE_URL` and sets `ssl: { rejectUnauthorized: false }` for RDS hosts when TLS is required.

## GitHub Pages

- Variable: `VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://<api-host>/api` (HTTPS, must end with `/api`)
- `CORS_ORIGIN` on API must match the browser origin of the Pages site

## Optional CP-SAT

- **Lambda:** `docs/AWS_LAMBDA_CPSAT.md` — set `CP_SAT_SOLVER_URL` on EC2; Lambda does not use RDS
- **Sidecar container:** `docs/AWS_CP_SAT.md`
- Default production: legacy engine when `CP_SAT_SOLVER_URL` is empty

